# Ye and Ghassemi (2018), specimen SW-T2.
#
# Units: m.
# Geometry: length = 0.13270, diameter = 0.05052.
#
# FRACTURE ANGLE: 30 degrees, NOT the 31 degrees printed in Table 1 of the paper.
#
# CORRECTION -- branch fix/physics-verification-audit.  This journal previously used
# 31 degrees (z_high = 0.1083896997, z_low = 0.0243103003), faithfully reproducing
# Table 1.  That is exactly the problem: the paper's own data was reduced at 30 deg.
#
# Table 2 reports both sigma'_n and tau at eleven hold stages.  With sigma_3 = 30 MPa
# and Pp = (Pi + Po)/2 these are two functions of the single unknown sigma_d, so
# their ratio fixes the angle:
#     tan(theta) = (sigma'_n - sigma_3 + Pp) / tau
# For SW-T2 this returns
#     loading   0.5775 0.5773 0.5774 0.5774 0.5774 0.5771
#     unloading 0.5775 0.5775 0.5772 0.5775 0.5773
# i.e. tan(30 deg) = 0.57735 at every stage, to four significant figures.
# tan(31 deg) = 0.60086 appears nowhere in the data.  The same test returns the
# tabulated angle to the same precision for SW-T1 (32), SW-S3 (29) and SW-S4 (30),
# so this is specific to SW-T2 -- either a typographical error in Table 1, or a
# reduction performed at 30 degrees.  Either way the model must use 30, because 31
# puts it on a stress path the published data was never on.
# See doc/theory/orca_czm_theory.md, Supplement.
#
# What the old 31-degree plane cost, at a given differential stress sigma_d:
#     tau      = sigma_d sin(th)cos(th) :  0.441474 vs 0.433013  -> 2.0% HIGH
#     sigma'_n deviatoric part          :  0.265264 vs 0.250000  -> 6.1% HIGH
#
# Corrected plane, centred at z = h/2 = 0.06635, at x = +/- r = 0.02526:
#     z = h/2 +/- r cot(30 deg) = 0.06635 +/- 0.0437516034
#     z_high = 0.1101016034      z_low = 0.0225983966
#
# AFTER REGENERATING, update the source coordinates in both SW-T2 decks (boreholes
# 6 mm inside the sidewall, x = +/- 0.019260):
#     source_in   coord = '-0.019260000 0.0 0.032990701'    (was 0.034295977)
#     source_out  coord = ' 0.019260000 0.0 0.099709299'    (was 0.098404023)
# Run meshes/apply_30deg_source_coords.py; see meshes/README_fracture_angle.md.
#
# Expected fracture_interface area after the split: 4.0091e-3 m^2.
# NOTE axial_pres_final was gated on the old 31-degree geometry and will need a
# ~2% trim; re-gate it with a short run before submitting production jobs.
#
# This journal preserves the SW-S4 construction order, block IDs, nodeset IDs,
# and names so it can be used by the same MOOSE mesh-generator workflow.

reset

create Cylinder height 0.13270 radius 0.02526
move Volume 1 z 0.06635 include_merged

create vertex location 0.02526 0.02526 0.1101016034
create vertex location 0.02526 -0.02526 0.1101016034
create vertex location -0.02526 -0.02526 0.0225983966
webcut volume 1 with plane vertex 3 vertex 4 vertex 5
delete vertex 3 4 5

webcut volume all with plane xplane imprint merge
webcut volume all with plane yplane imprint merge
imprint all
merge all

vol all size auto factor 1   # 5 -> ye_ghassemi_2018_SWT2_size_5.e
volume all scheme polyhedron
mesh volume all

block 1 add volume 2 4 8 6
block 1 name "top_block"

block 2 add volume 1 3 5 7
block 2 name "bottom_block"

# Uncomment both lines for the quadratic-element variant used by the HEX27
# SW-S4 journals. Leave commented for the first-order/low-mesh variant.
# block 1 element type HEX27
# block 2 element type HEX27

nodeset 1 add surface 36 56 63 42
nodeset 1 name "top_nodeset"

nodeset 2 add surface 28 30 50 48
nodeset 2 name "bottom_nodeset"

nodeset 3 add surface 33 43 61 51 25 35 57 47
nodeset 3 name "sides_nodeset"

nodeset 4 add surface 26 46 53 32
nodeset 4 name "fracture_interface"

nodeset 5 add vertex 27 34 41 48
nodeset 5 name "no_disp_x"

nodeset 6 add vertex 10 11 18 19
nodeset 6 name "no_disp_y"

# Uncomment to export automatically when this journal is run from its mesh
# directory.
# export mesh "ye2018_sw_t2_low_mesh.e" overwrite
